export default function Page3(){return <><Frame0 /><div className={"scroll-progress"} data-scroll-progress={""} aria-hidden={"true"}></div><main id={"main"} x-data={""} {...{"x-on:cart-added.window": "$store.cart.count++"}}><section className={"custom-ph"} aria-labelledby={"hm-page-title"}><div className={"container"}><nav aria-label={"Breadcrumb"} data-anim={"fade"}><ol className={"breadcrumb breadcrumb--sm"}><li className={"breadcrumb-item"}><a href={"#page=demo-handmade-store-1"}>{"Home"}</a></li><li className={"breadcrumb-item"}><a href={"#page=demo-handmade-store-1-blog"}>{"Journal"}</a></li><li className={"breadcrumb-item"} aria-current={"page"}>{"Care"}</li></ol></nav><div className={"mt-8 grid items-end gap-x-16 gap-y-10 lg:grid-cols-12"}><div className={"lg:col-span-7"} data-anim={"fade-up"}><p className={"custom-kicker"}>{"Care · 5 min read · October 21, 2027"}</p><h1 id={"hm-page-title"} className={"custom-ph-title custom-ph-title--lg"}>{"How to wash linen so it softens for decades"}</h1><p className={"custom-sec-lead"}>{"Cool water, no softener and a line in the sun. Clara Farrow has woven linen in Astoria for eleven years; this is the care she gives her own napkins."}</p><div className={"mt-7 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-8 gap-y-4"}><span className={"custom-post-by"}><img src={"https://draftmango.com/framo/assets/media/placeholder/320x320.svg"} alt={""} width={"320"} height={"320"} />{"Written by Clara Farrow, Linden Loom"}</span><a href={"#checklist"} className={"custom-text-link"}>{"Jump to the Checklist "}<i className={"ph ph-arrow-down"} aria-hidden={"true"}></i></a></div></div><figure className={"custom-shot custom-post-cover lg:col-span-5"} data-anim={"unveil-up"} data-anim-delay={"120"}><img src={"https://draftmango.com/framo/assets/media/placeholder/809x814.svg"} alt={"Natural linen tablecloths drying on a line in a sunny garden"} width={"809"} height={"814"} fetchPriority={"high"} /></figure></div><ol className={"custom-glance mt-12"} role={"list"} data-anim-stagger={"70"}><li data-anim={"fade-up"}><a href={"#step-1"}><span>{"01"}</span>{"Wash cool and gentle"}</a></li><li data-anim={"fade-up"}><a href={"#step-2"}><span>{"02"}</span>{"Skip the softener"}</a></li><li data-anim={"fade-up"}><a href={"#step-3"}><span>{"03"}</span>{"Dry on a line"}</a></li><li data-anim={"fade-up"}><a href={"#step-4"}><span>{"04"}</span>{"Iron damp, or not at all"}</a></li><li data-anim={"fade-up"}><a href={"#step-5"}><span>{"05"}</span>{"Store it loosely"}</a></li></ol></div></section><div><nav className={"page-nav custom-page-nav"} data-page-nav={""} aria-label={"Guide contents"}><div className={"container page-nav-inner"}><a href={"#step-1"} className={"page-nav-link is-active"}>{"01 · Wash"}</a><a href={"#step-2"} className={"page-nav-link"}>{"02 · Softener"}</a><a href={"#step-3"} className={"page-nav-link"}>{"03 · Dry"}</a><a href={"#step-4"} className={"page-nav-link"}>{"04 · Iron"}</a><a href={"#step-5"} className={"page-nav-link"}>{"05 · Store"}</a><a href={"#checklist"} className={"page-nav-link"}>{"Checklist"}</a></div></nav><article className={"article-body custom-article py-16 md:py-24"}><p className={"custom-article-lead"}>{"New linen feels a little stiff, like a good pair of jeans. That is the flax fiber, long and strong, and it is exactly why linen lasts. Every wash breaks the fibers in a little more, until one day your napkins drape like old cotton and still won’t wear through."}</p><p>{"You don’t need special products to get there. You need to stop doing three things most of us do to towels, and give linen a little sun."}</p><h2 id={"step-1"} className={"page-nav-section"}><span className={"custom-article-step"}>{"Step 01"}</span>{"Wash cool and gentle"}</h2><p>{"Wash at 85°F or below on a gentle cycle, with a mild liquid detergent and plenty of room in the drum. Hot water and a packed machine are what crease linen for good — the fibers need space to move."}</p><div className={"article-offset"}><figure><div className={"img-frame img-frame-rounded aspect-[4/3]"}><img className={"h-full w-full object-cover"} src={"https://draftmango.com/framo/assets/media/placeholder/850x1138.svg"} alt={"Clara Farrow at her floor loom threaded with natural linen"} width={"850"} height={"1138"} loading={"lazy"} decoding={"async"} /></div></figure><p className={"article-note"}><b>{"From the loom"}</b>{"Clara weaves with European flax and washes every finished napkin twice before it ships, so yours arrive already a little soft."}</p></div><h2 id={"step-2"} className={"page-nav-section"}><span className={"custom-article-step"}>{"Step 02"}</span>{"Skip the softener"}</h2><p>{"Fabric softener coats the fiber in a waxy film. Linen loses the thing it is best at — drinking up water — and slowly turns stiff and dull. If the water where you live is hard, half a cup of white vinegar in the rinse does the job better."}</p><div className={"alert alert-lg alert-primary custom-alert"}><i className={"ph ph-drop-half alert-icon"} aria-hidden={"true"}></i><p className={"alert-content"}><strong>{"Stains?"}</strong>{" Blot, don’t rub. Cold water and a little dish soap lift most food stains; leave red wine to soak overnight in cold water before you wash."}</p></div><h2 id={"step-3"} className={"page-nav-section"}><span className={"custom-article-step"}>{"Step 03"}</span>{"Dry on a line"}</h2><p>{"Shake each piece out hard, pull the hems straight and hang it in the shade or a gentle sun. Linen dries fast. If you must use a dryer, use low heat and take it out while it is still a touch damp."}</p><div className={"article-offset article-offset--right"}><figure><div className={"img-frame img-frame-rounded aspect-[4/3]"}><img className={"h-full w-full object-cover"} src={"https://draftmango.com/framo/assets/media/placeholder/1600x1200.svg"} alt={"Folded stonewashed linen napkins tied with cotton string"} width={"1600"} height={"1200"} loading={"lazy"} decoding={"async"} /></div></figure><p className={"article-note"}><b>{"The rumpled look"}</b>{"Most of our customers never iron their napkins again after the first month. A loose fold straight off the line is how linen is meant to look."}</p></div><h2 id={"step-4"} className={"page-nav-section"}><span className={"custom-article-step"}>{"Step 04"}</span>{"Iron damp, or not at all"}</h2><p>{"If you like a crisp tablecloth for a dinner, iron it while it is still damp, on the reverse, at a medium-high setting. Bone dry linen fights back; damp linen gives in."}</p><h2 id={"step-5"} className={"page-nav-section"}><span className={"custom-article-step"}>{"Step 05"}</span>{"Store it loosely"}</h2><p>{"Fold loosely and change the folds now and then, so the creases never set into lines. Keep linen somewhere that breathes — a drawer or a basket, never a sealed plastic box."}</p><div id={"checklist"} className={"page-nav-section custom-checklist"} x-data={"{ done: 0 }"}><div className={"flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-4"}><div><p className={"custom-kicker"}>{"Pin It by the Machine"}</p><p className={"custom-h3 mt-2"}>{"The linen checklist"}</p></div><p className={"m-0 font-semibold"}><span x-text={"done"}>{"0"}</span>{" / 6"}</p></div><div className={"progress progress--sm mt-5"}><div className={"progress-bar"} {...{"x-bind:style": "`width: ${done / 6 * 100}%`"}} style={{"width": "0%"}}></div></div><div className={"mt-6 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2"}><label className={"form-check"}><input type={"checkbox"} className={"form-check-input"} {...{"x-on:change": "done += $event.target.checked ? 1 : -1"}} /><span className={"form-check-label"}>{"Cool water, 85°F or below"}</span></label><label className={"form-check"}><input type={"checkbox"} className={"form-check-input"} {...{"x-on:change": "done += $event.target.checked ? 1 : -1"}} /><span className={"form-check-label"}>{"Gentle cycle, half a load"}</span></label><label className={"form-check"}><input type={"checkbox"} className={"form-check-input"} {...{"x-on:change": "done +=